  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward if recent sentiment is positive (e.g., >0.00) and model overestimates prices — indicates bullish sentiment may be overblown.",
    "Reduce forecast overshoot after sharp price spikes — model tends to overreact and overcorrects in 30-day horizon.",
    "Apply mean reversion bias: if 30-day forecast is significantly above recent 18-day average, reduce by 5–10% to account for volatility decay.",
    "If sentiment is neutral (0.00), prioritize historical mean reversion over trend-following — avoid overconfidence in short-term momentum.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, penalize high variance in early days (e.g., days 1–5) — model often overestimates near-term volatility and underestimates mean reversion."
